I just "finished" a patch to the wishing code that lets the player wish
for --- and get --- objects already existing in monsters' inventories,
as described back in 2003 here:
http://groups.google.com/groups?selm=Pine.LNX.4.55L-032.0308051326410.11206@unix50.andrew.cmu.edu

   That is, if a dwarf is whaling on you with a pickaxe and you /really/
have no better way out, just #rub that lamp and wish for "the dwarf's
pickaxe". "e - a pickaxe. The dwarf looks startled!"

   I'm sure the patch is full of bugs; and right now it doesn't really
do anything terribly clever in terms of gameplay, IMO.

   Critiques and ideas for expansion welcome. Some I've already thought
of, with comments:

   * Wishing for items that are currently on other levels (e.g., "my box
named Stash"). I'd like to do this one, but it would be a real pain,
because levels other than the current one are stored on disk.

   * Wishing for named items without a monster "owner" (e.g., "Magicbane"
when it's just been stolen by a nymph). Also a good idea, and doable,
but I think it would need some more infrastructure.

   * An even better way out of that jam: wish for "the dwarf's corpse"!
Combine with previous ideas to get Fluffy's corpse for reanimation
(whether Fluffy is dead or not, I suppose!).

   * Wishing for things on the ground; but how do you specify them?
"That cockatrice corpse"?

   * Conditional patching to let wizards wish for Brad's pit. :)  I used
it as an example in the comments, but it doesn't actually work yet.

   * Wishing for "Croesus' gold" could get you the contents of any
vaults on the current level. I dunno about this one, though.

